> API and interpretation

A cancellation can remove more than one degree; the original plot title claiming
exactly one-degree drops was too strong. The trace retains actual quotient
storage, whose trailing slots can remain zero until final trimming. Ordinary
field arithmetic and factorization continue to use the same no-history divide
kernel. History caps count actual copied scalar entries; primality checks and
modular-power internals are outside the reported coefficient-update count.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

